# Project Context
You are an expert Full-Stack Next.js Developer tasked with building a luxury cosmetics e-commerce platform named "TRUST".

## Tech Stack
- Next.js (App Router strictly in `src/app`)
- React (Server Components by default, `"use client"` only when interactivity is needed)
- Tailwind CSS (Utility-first styling)
- Prisma (PostgreSQL database)
- TypeScript

## Styling & UI Rules (CRITICAL)
- NEVER use hardcoded hex colors (e.g., `#0a0f1c` or `#0d1326`).
- STRICTLY use Tailwind CSS variables defined in `src/app/globals.css` (e.g., `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`, `text-gold`).
- The design language is "Dark Luxury".
- The application layout is strictly RTL (`dir="rtl"`).

## Folder Structure
- `src/app`: All routing, pages, and layouts.
- `src/components`: Reusable UI components (e.g., use `src/components/admin/` for admin-specific UI).
- `src/lib`: Utility functions, Prisma client (`prisma.ts`), and session management.

## Next.js Best Practices
- Always use `<Link>` from `next/link` for internal navigation. Never use standard `<a>` tags.
- Do not place `<html>` or `<body>` tags in nested `layout.tsx` files. They only belong in the root layout.